  "notes": "がたがた is an onomatopoeic word with multiple related meanings.\n\nSOUND USES:\n- {窓|まど}ががたがた{鳴|な}る: window rattling\n- {歯|は}ががたがた{震|ふる}える: teeth chattering (from cold/fear)\n\nCONDITION USES:\n- がたがたの{道|みち}: bumpy road\n- がたがたの{机|つくえ}: rickety desk\n\nCOMPLAINING USE:\n- がたがた{言|い}う: to complain, nag\n- Common in casual/frustrated speech",
